 "description": "ReplyQuality v1 criteria (P0 of OPEN_ENDED_SELF_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN_20261010.md). A REPORT-ONLY measure of whether a reply fits the turn it answers: the inbound's act (greeting / question / imperative / statement), whether a question is addressed to the agent, the reply's surface class, topical overlap, and whether a content reply is a dictionary-style definition. Scores 2 appropriate, 1 acceptable-minimal, 0 inappropriate. It is a proxy; its agreement with human labels is the Q0 gate. Criteria are data so a later phase can propose changes to them (P6); it gates nothing in v1. v1.1.0 (2026-10-10, before any labels; defects found on the production stream, dialogues 0-9, not the held-out set): whether a reply is about the agent is read from its FIRST sentence (a first-person token deep in a quoted passage made it self_content); 'I don't hold anything about X' is honest not-knowing (gap_floor); a rhetorical tag ('I know, right?') does not make a turn a question.",
